title: Free-hosting site named after a brand asks for credentials
severity: high
score: 50
tags: phishing, brand-impersonation, free-hosting
attack: T1583.006, T1656, T1566.002
description: A page on a free hosting or site-builder platform asks for a password, sign-in
  name, card, code or recovery phrase. Its tenant name carries a brand (microsoftaccount-
  kit.<builder>, ledger-live-kit.pages.dev). The page itself need not name the brand.
  Builder forms often have no real password field.
---
// A free hosting tenant whose name spells a brand, asking for a secret, not allowlisted.
brand_labels
| where isnotempty(prompt) and not allowlisted(host)
| project brand, keyword, host, platform, prompt
